IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-nouns`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`

-- Interpretation Act 1984 (Western Australia) -- PART III: COMMENCEMENT AND CITATION, the parts that are not
-- time computations.  The time rules of ss 20, 21, 22, 23, 25(3) and 27 are in wa-interpretation-time.l4; this
-- module holds ss 25(1), (2), (4), (5) and 26.  Section 24 is shown as deleted in the text.

§ `Part III -- Commencement and citation`

§§ `25. Some powers in an Act may be exercised before it commences`

-- Section 25(1) and (2): where a provision of an Act does not commence on the passing of the Act and would, if
-- it had commenced, confer a power to make an instrument of a legislative or administrative character, give or
-- serve a notice or other document, appoint a person to a specified office, establish a specified body, or do any
-- other thing for the purposes of the Act (or, under (2), would amend another Act so that a provision of that
-- other Act would confer such a power), the power may be exercised at any time after the passing of the Act to
-- the extent that it is necessary or expedient for bringing the Act or its provisions into operation, or giving
-- full effect to them.  "Necessary or expedient" is a judgment: a plain input.
-- src:386 | (1) Where a provision of an Act does not commence on the passing of the Act and that provision would, if it had commenced, confer power to —
-- src:387 | (a) make an instrument of a legislative or administrative character; or
-- src:388 | (b) give or serve a notice or other document; or
-- src:389 | (c) appoint a person to a specified office; or
-- src:390 | (d) establish a specified body of persons, whether incorporated or not; or
-- src:391 | (e) do any other thing for the purposes of the Act,
-- src:392 | then the power may, notwithstanding that that provision has not commenced, but subject to subsections (3) and (4), be exercised at any time after the passing of the Act to the extent that it is necessary or expedient for the purpose of bringing the Act, or provisions of the Act, into operation, or giving full effect to the Act, or provisions of the Act, when or after that provision commences.
-- src:393 | (2) Where —
-- src:394 | (a) a provision of an Act does not commence on the passing of the Act and the provision would, if it had commenced, amend another Act; and
-- src:395 | (b) a provision of that other Act would, if the firstmentioned provision had commenced, confer power to —
-- src:396 | (i) make an instrument of a legislative or administrative character; or
-- src:397 | (ii) give or serve a notice or other document; or
-- src:398 | (iii) appoint a person to a specified office; or
-- src:399 | (iv) establish a specified body of persons whether incorporated or not; or
-- src:400 | (v) do any other thing for the purposes of that other Act,
-- src:401 | then the power may, notwithstanding that the firstmentioned provision has not commenced, but subject to subsections (3) and (4), be exercised at any time after the passing of the Act in which the firstmentioned provision is contained to the extent that it is necessary or expedient for the purpose of giving full effect to that other Act, or provisions of that other Act, when or after the firstmentioned provision commences.
@ref s 25(1) (src:386-392)
@ref s 25(2) (src:393-401)
GIVEN `the provision commences on the passing of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision would itself confer the power if it had commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision would amend another Act so that a provision of that Act would confer the power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is of a kind the section lists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act has been passed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exercise is necessary or expedient for bringing the Act or its provisions into operation, or giving full effect to them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the power may be exercised before the provision commences` `the provision commences on the passing of the Act` `the provision would itself confer the power if it had commenced` `the provision would amend another Act so that a provision of that Act would confer the power` `the power is of a kind the section lists` `the Act has been passed` `the exercise is necessary or expedient for bringing the Act or its provisions into operation, or giving full effect to them` MEANS
        (NOT `the provision commences on the passing of the Act`)
    AND (   `the provision would itself confer the power if it had commenced`
         OR `the provision would amend another Act so that a provision of that Act would confer the power`)
    AND `the power is of a kind the section lists`
    AND `the Act has been passed`
    AND `the exercise is necessary or expedient for bringing the Act or its provisions into operation, or giving full effect to them`

-- Section 25(4): a person appointed (or a body established) under a power exercised early may act in that
-- office (or the body may meet and perform its functions) only for a purpose referred to in s 25(1) or (2); and
-- the term of office does not begin until the relevant provision commences.
-- src:406 | (4) Where a power to appoint a person to a specified office, or to establish a specified body of persons, is exercised as provided in subsection (1) or (2), the person so appointed may act in that office, or, as the case may be, the body so established may meet and perform and exercise its functions, duties, and powers, but only for a purpose referred to in subsection (1) or (2) (whichever of those subsections is applicable); and for the purposes of any provision as to the duration of the term of office of the person or a member of the body, that term does not begin until the relevant provision referred to in subsection (1) or (2), as the case may be, commences.
@ref s 25(4) (src:406)
GIVEN `the purpose is one referred to in subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointee may act in the office, or the body may meet and perform its functions` `the purpose is one referred to in subsection (1) or (2)` MEANS
    `the purpose is one referred to in subsection (1) or (2)`

@ref s 25(4) (src:406)
GIVEN `the day the relevant provision commences` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest day the term of office of an early appointee begins` `the day the relevant provision commences` MEANS
    `the day the relevant provision commences`

-- Section 25(5): subject to s 3(3), the section applies to Acts passed after the commencement of this Act; for an
-- Act passed before it, the section says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:407 | (5) Subject to section 3(3), this section applies to Acts passed after the commencement of this Act 1.
@ref s 25(5) (src:407)
GIVEN `the day the Act was passed` IS A DATE
      `it continues or directly amends, but does not repeal entirely, the text of an existing written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 25 applies to the Act` `the day the Act was passed` `it continues or directly amends, but does not repeal entirely, the text of an existing written law` MEANS
    IF `counts as passed or made after the commencement for ss 17, 25, 43(6), 50 and 64` `the day the Act was passed` `it continues or directly amends, but does not repeal entirely, the text of an existing written law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `26. Citation of written laws`

DECLARE `Form of citation` IS ONE OF
    `the short title or the citation given to it or by which it was made citable`
    `the year in which it was passed and its number among the Acts of that year`
    `the Part, section, regulation, rule, clause or other division in which a provision is contained`
    `some other form of citation`

-- Section 26(1) and (2): it is sufficient for all purposes to cite a written law by its short title or citation
-- or, for an Act, by the year in which it was passed and its number among that year's Acts; and a provision may
-- be cited by the Part, section, regulation, rule, clause or other division containing it.  The year-and-number
-- form is given for Acts only: for subsidiary legislation, and for any other form, the Act says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:409 | (1) Where a written law is referred to, it shall be sufficient for all purposes to cite or refer to that written law by —
-- src:410 | (a) the short title or the citation (if any) given to it or by which it was made citable; or
-- src:411 | (b) in the case of an Act, the year in which it was passed and its number among the Acts of that year.
-- src:412 | (2) A provision of a written law may be cited by reference to the Part, section, regulation, rule, clause or other division of the written law in which the provision is contained.
@ref s 26(1) (src:409-411)
@ref s 26(2) (src:412)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of citation`
      kind IS A `Kind of written law`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a citation is sufficient for all purposes` form kind MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `the short title or the citation given to it or by which it was made citable` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the year in which it was passed and its number among the Acts of that year` THEN
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `an Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `subsidiary legislation` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the Part, section, regulation, rule, clause or other division in which a provision is contained` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `some other form of citation` THEN NOTHING

-- Section 26(3): the citation of or reference to a written law is in all cases to be made in accordance with an
-- official version of the law under the Legislation Act 2021.  Whether the version is official is a borrowed fact.
-- src:413 | (3) The citation of or reference to a written law is in all cases to be made in accordance with an official version of the law under the Legislation Act 2021.
@ref s 26(3) (src:413)
GIVEN `it is made in accordance with an official version of the law under the Legislation Act 2021` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a citation or reference is made as the Act requires` `it is made in accordance with an official version of the law under the Legislation Act 2021` MEANS
    `it is made in accordance with an official version of the law under the Legislation Act 2021`
